{"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Framework","title":"GoogleAnalyticsEncoding","modules":[{"name":"GoogleAnalyticsEncoding"}],"symbolKind":"module","role":"collection","externalID":"GoogleAnalyticsEncoding"},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Sending-to-Google-Analytics","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/googleAnalytics(measurementID:apiSecret:region:plan:backoff:clock:now:)","doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/googleAnalytics(measurementID:apiSecret:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:now:)","doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsRegion","doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsSetupError"],"title":"Sending to Google Analytics"},{"anchor":"Encoding-batches","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder"],"title":"Encoding batches"},{"anchor":"Records-left-out","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsEncodingError"],"title":"Records left out"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records from a server to a Google Analytics 4 web or data stream through the Measurement Protocol."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/googleanalyticsencoding"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/googleAnalytics(measurementID:apiSecret:region:plan:backoff:clock:now:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"makes an ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","type":"reference"},{"text":") for a Google Analytics 4 stream in one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"call. It checks the measurement ID and the API secret, and posts to the Measurement Protocol’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"\/mp\/collect","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" endpoint of the region (","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsRegion","type":"reference"},{"text":") with a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder","type":"reference"},{"text":". It splits each batch to the Measurement Protocol’s limits","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","type":"reference"},{"text":"): 25 events and 100 KB a request. A batch with no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record the encoder can write, an empty one included, makes no request. The destination retries no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"response, a 5xx, 408 and 429, and drops and reports any other status. No trace context is sent.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"import Traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" leaves this module out; import it on its own.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"The-API-secret-stays-on-a-server","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"The API secret stays on a server"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Measurement Protocol takes only requests that carry one of the stream’s API secrets, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"anyone holding that secret can send events to the property. Google’s docs say not to expose it in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an app, and an app’s binary can be read by anyone who installs it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"So the whole module is compiled for macOS and Linux alone, where a server runs. An app for iOS,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"iPadOS, tvOS, watchOS, visionOS or Mac Catalyst that calls the factory, or names the encoder, fails"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to compile. A Mac app, AppKit or SwiftUI, compiles the factory as a Mac server does, but the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"factory refuses it at run time: it throws "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsSetupError\/appBundle"},{"type":"text","text":" when the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"process’s main bundle is an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".app"},{"type":"text","text":" or an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".appex"},{"type":"text","text":". Nothing stops a Mac app from building an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" with this encoder and an endpoint it writes itself, secret and all, so don’t."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The secret is also in the query of every request’s URL. Don’t log the destination, its requests or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a transport’s URLs.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The factory throws ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsSetupError","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" for an empty measurement ID, for one that isn’t","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"G-","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" followed by uppercase letters and digits, and for an empty API secret. The region has no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"default: ","type":"text"},{"code":".global","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is Google’s default endpoint, and ","type":"text"},{"code":".eu","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" has Google collect the data in the EU.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Getting-an-apps-events-to-Google-Analytics","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Getting an app’s events to Google Analytics"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An app’s events reach Google Analytics through a server of yours: the app sends them there, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the server makes this destination and hands it the records. Traffluent doesn’t provide that server"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"yet. TraffluentCollector receives an app’s batches, but it doesn’t forward them to Google"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Analytics, and Traffluent has no decoder that turns a collector batch back into records."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Until it does, the server’s job is:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Read each event the app sent (its name, version, identifier, timestamp, properties and session)","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and decode it into the same ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" type the app tracked, from a module the app and the server","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"share.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Remake its "},{"code":"EventRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"code":"EventRecord(id:event:timestamp:sourceLocation:context:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"app’s identifier and timestamp, and a context whose "},{"code":"SessionKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the app’s session."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Hand each batch of records to the destination’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"receive(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"orderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Don’t track the events again through a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Tracker","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"code":".sessions()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on the server. That tracker","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"would give every event the server’s own session, so every user of the app would arrive in Google","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Analytics as one ","type":"text"},{"code":"client_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A server that tracks its own events, rather than an app’s, uses a tracker as any app does:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import HTTPDestinations","import GoogleAnalyticsEncoding","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let googleAnalytics = try HTTPDestination.googleAnalytics(","    measurementID: measurementID,  \/\/ the web or data stream's, G-…","    apiSecret: apiSecret,  \/\/ from the server's configuration, never an app's","    region: .global,  \/\/ or .eu, to have Google collect the data in the EU","    plan: plan)","\/\/ A server tracking its own events: its sessions are the server's.","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: googleAnalytics)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"anchor":"What-Google-Analytics-receives","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"What Google Analytics receives"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each request holds one client’s events, as the Measurement Protocol takes one "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"client_id"},{"type":"text","text":" a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"request. The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"client_id"},{"type":"text","text":" is the record’s session, from the sessions enricher, written as the two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"halves of its UUID in decimal, joined by a period, the form the Measurement Protocol asks for. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record with no session is sent under its own record identifier, in a request of its own. Each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"event’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"session_id"},{"type":"text","text":" parameter is the session’s start in Unix milliseconds, so Google Analytics"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"groups the session’s events, and its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"timestamp_micros"},{"type":"text","text":" is the record’s timestamp. Every request"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sends ad consent as denied, so Google uses none of the events for advertising."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"No ","type":"text"},{"code":"user_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", user properties, location, IP address, device or user agent is sent, and no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"advertising identifier. The record’s vendor identifier, trace context and standard context aren’t","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sent either. Google Analytics counts a user per ","type":"text"},{"code":"client_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so each session is one user in its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reports, and so is each record sent without a session.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"engagement_time_msec"},{"type":"text","text":" is sent, as Traffluent doesn’t measure engagement. Without it the events"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"don’t count toward engagement time or engaged sessions, and the Realtime and Users reports can show"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"no users while events arrive. Check the event counts, not the user counts, to see that the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"destination works."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan"},{"type":"text","text":" the encoder is made with,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and become the event’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"params"},{"type":"text","text":". A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Google Analytics takes only strings, numbers and booleans, so a nested value is spread into a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"parameter for each value it holds, named after its path joined by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cart_size"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tags_0"},{"type":"text","text":"), and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"null"},{"type":"text","text":" is left out."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Records-sent-twice","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Records sent twice"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The Measurement Protocol has no field that identifies an event, so Google Analytics can’t tell a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"repeat from a new event, and counts every one it receives. A record is sent more than once when a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"request is retried after Google stored it but the answer was lost, when a delivery sends a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"cancelled batch again, and when a store redelivers records after a relaunch. Each such record is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"counted twice in Google Analytics.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Records-left-out","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Records left out"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out and the rest of the batch is sent:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one the plan doesn’t describe, whose event isn’t "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"type":"text","text":", or that holds a value JSON can’t;"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one whose event name, or a parameter’s name, is longer than 40 bytes, doesn’t start with a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"letter, or holds anything but letters, numbers and "},{"code":"_","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":";"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"one whose event name Google Analytics keeps (","type":"text"},{"code":"session_start","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"first_visit","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"error","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and the rest","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of its reserved names), or takes only from an app stream (","type":"text"},{"code":"screen_view","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"ad_impression","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"in_app_purchase","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":");","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one with a parameter Google Analytics keeps (a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"firebase_"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ga_"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"google_"},{"type":"text","text":" prefix) or named"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"session_id"},{"type":"text","text":", which the encoder writes;"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"one of more than 25 parameters, counting ","type":"text"},{"code":"session_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or with a string longer than 100 bytes;","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"one tracked more than 71 hours before the batch is encoded, or more than 15 minutes after it,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and one whose timestamp has no microseconds form;","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"one too large for a request.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Google Analytics wouldn’t refuse such an event: it answers 2xx either way. Under its default,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"relaxed validation it stores the event without the parameter that breaks a rule, or under a name"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it never checked, so the report would hold an event other than the one tracked. The encoder leaves"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the record out and reports it instead. A Google Analytics 360 property takes values of up to 500"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"characters, but the encoder holds every property to the standard 100 bytes."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The destination reports each as ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", a ","type":"text"},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" whose reason is a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsEncodingError"},{"text":". The encoder logs a notice for each event and property of the plan","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"named as Google Analytics refuses when the destination is made; rename such an event or property,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"raising the event’s version, to send it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"What-the-Measurement-Protocol-doesnt-report","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"What the Measurement Protocol doesn’t report"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Measurement Protocol answers 2xx to every request it receives, including one it can’t read and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one whose events it doesn’t store. A wrong measurement ID or API secret is answered 2xx with nothing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stored, so check the property’s Realtime event counts after setting the destination up. Google’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"validation server, "},{"code":"\/debug\/mp\/collect","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", checks a body’s shape but not the measurement ID or the API"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"secret, so a body it accepts can still be stored nowhere. A record older than 72 hours is stored as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"if it happened 72 hours ago, so the encoder leaves out one older than 71 hours, the hour to spare"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for the request to reach Google and clocks that disagree. A request is encoded once and retried as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it is, so the encoder gives each request a deadline 71 hours after its oldest record was tracked. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"request still failing by then isn’t sent again: the destination drops the whole request, its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"younger records too, and reports it on "},{"code":"dropReports","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"HTTPDropReport.deadlineExceeded(deadline:recordIDs:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", with every one of its records’ identifiers."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"To send to PostHog, Amplitude, Mixpanel or Segment, use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PostHogEncoding"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AmplitudeEncoding"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MixpanelEncoding"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SegmentSpecEncoding"},{"text":" instead.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers what Google Analytics receives, and why, in more detail."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/documentation/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder/batchLimit":{"abstract":[{"text":"The Measurement Protocol’s limits on one request: 25 events and 100,000 bytes of body, an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"event’s included.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/googleanalyticsencoding\/googleanalyticsbatchencoder\/batchlimit","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"batchLimit"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12PropertyJSON10BatchLimitV","text":"BatchLimit"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","title":"batchLimit"},"doc://GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/documentation/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/GoogleAnalyticsRegion":{"abstract":[{"text":"Where Google Analytics collects a stream’s events, which decides the Measurement Protocol","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"endpoint they are posted to.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/googleanalyticsencoding\/googleanalyticsregion","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"GoogleAnalyticsRegion"}],"title":"GoogleAnalyticsRegion","identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsRegion","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"GoogleAnalyticsRegion"}]},"doc://GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/documentation/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination/googleAnalytics(measurementID:apiSecret:region:plan:backoff:clock:now:)":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A destination on a server that sends batches to the Google Analytics web or data stream of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"measurementID","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", authenticated by its "},{"code":"apiSecret","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", with "},{"code":"URLSession.shared","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", retrying a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"send that fails for now with the waits of "},{"code":"backoff","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on "},{"code":"clock","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/googleanalyticsencoding\/httpdestinations\/httpdestination\/googleanalytics(measurementid:apisecret:region:plan:backoff:clock:now:)","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"googleAnalytics"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"measurementID"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"apiSecret"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"region"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:23GoogleAnalyticsEncoding0aB6RegionO","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"GoogleAnalyticsRegion"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"plan"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:13TrackingPlans0A4PlanV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"TrackingPlan"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"backoff"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations18ExponentialBackoffV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ExponentialBackoff"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"clock"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency5ClockP","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Clock"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s8DurationV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Duration"},{"kind":"text","text":">, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"now"},{"kind":"text","text":": () -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:20FoundationEssentials4DateV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Date"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:23GoogleAnalyticsEncoding0aB10SetupErrorO","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"GoogleAnalyticsSetupError"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations15HTTPDestinationV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"HTTPDestination"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"preciseIdentifier":